WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:08.294
In the Encyclopedia of Triangle Centers, the Isogonal Conjugate is the fundamental angular reflection of triangle geometry.

2
00:00:08.294 --> 00:00:20.010
Reflecting the three cevians of a point P across the interior angle bisectors A X one, B X one, and C X one yields three new concurrent lines meeting at its isogonal conjugate P star.

3
00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:31.605
In homogeneous trilinear coordinates, isogonal conjugation simply takes the reciprocal of each distance: alpha, beta, gamma maps to one over alpha, one over beta, one over gamma.

4
00:00:31.605 --> 00:00:35.309
Across Collection One, the Incenter X one is self-isogonal.

5
00:00:35.309 --> 00:00:42.027
The Centroid X two and Symmedian Point X six are isogonal conjugates, transforming medians into symmedians.

6
00:00:42.027 --> 00:00:50.000
And the Circumcenter X three and Orthocenter X four are isogonal conjugates, reflecting perpendicular bisectors into altitudes.

7
00:00:50.420 --> 00:01:03.140
Even the equilateral centers obey isogonal duality: the First and Second Fermat points X thirteen and X fourteen map directly to the First and Second Isodynamic points X fifteen and X sixteen.
